<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>Phenomena Incognita | Order of the Lion's Bell</title>
  <style>
    :root{
      --bg: #05060a;
      --panel: #0a0b12;
      --text: #ddd6c8;
      --muted: #b8ad97;
      --gold: #c9a45c;
      --gold-soft: rgba(201, 164, 92, 0.18);
      --line: rgba(201, 164, 92, 0.25);
      --heading: #e2c98d;
    }

    *{
      box-sizing: border-box;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
    }

    body{
      background: radial-gradient(circle at top, #0d1020 0%, var(--bg) 30%, var(--bg) 100%);
      color: var(--text);
      font-family: "Georgia", "Times New Roman", serif;
      line-height: 1.8;
    }

    


    main{
      max-width: 1100px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 70px 28px 100px;
    }

    .hero{
      text-align: center;
      margin-bottom: 56px;
    }

    .hero h1{
      color: var(--heading);
      font-size: clamp(2.3rem, 5vw, 4.3rem);
      font-style: italic;
      font-weight: 600;
      line-height: 1.15;
      text-shadow: 0 0 20px rgba(201, 164, 92, 0.2);
    }

    .hero .subtitle{
      margin-top: 14px;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 1rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    }


      .intro-line{
      max-width: 760px;
      margin: 28px auto 0;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-style: italic;
      font-size: 1rem;
    }

    .eyebrow{
      color: var(--muted);
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.18em;
      font-size: 0.78rem;
      margin-bottom: 14px;
    }

    .rule{
      width: 140px;
      height: 1px;
      background: var(--line);
      margin: 32px auto 0;
    }

    .page-grid{
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 0.8fr;
      gap: 30px;
      align-items: start;
    }

    .content-column{
      display: grid;
      gap: 28px;
    }

    .side-column{
      display: grid;
      gap: 24px;
    }

    .section,
    .side-card{
      background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255,255,255,0.01), rgba(255,255,255,0));
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      padding: 28px 26px;
    }

    .section h2,
    .side-card h3{
      color: var(--heading);
      font-size: 1.28rem;
      margin-bottom: 16px;
      font-weight: 600;
      letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    }

    .section p{
      color: var(--text);
      font-size: 1.02rem;
    }

    .section p + p{
      margin-top: 14px;
    }

    .section ul,
    .side-card ul{
      list-style: none;
      display: grid;
      gap: 12px;
    }

    .section li,
    .side-card li{
      position: relative;
      padding-left: 18px;
      color: var(--text);
    }




    .records{
      display: grid;
      gap: 16px;
      margin-top: 6px;
    }

    .record-block{
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      padding: 18px 18px 16px;
      background: rgba(201, 164, 92, 0.03);
    }

    .record-block h4{
      color: var(--heading);
      font-size: 1rem;
      margin-bottom: 8px;
      letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    }

    .record-block p{
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 0.97rem;
      margin: 0;
    }


    
    .tag{
      display: inline-block;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      color: var(--gold);
      padding: 5px 10px;
      margin: 6px 8px 0 0;
      font-size: 0.82rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.04em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }


    @media (max-width: 900px){
      .page-grid{
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }

      main{
        padding: 50px 18px 70px;
      }

      .section,
      .side-card{
        padding: 22px 18px;
      }
    }












  </style>
</head>





<body>
 
  <main>
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="eyebrow">Discipline of the Order</div>
      <h1>Phenomena Incognita</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">Anomalous Phenomena</p>
      <p class="intro-line">
        These matters are not to be believed without evidence, nor dismissed without examination.
      </p>
      <div class="rule"></div>
    </section>

    <div class="page-grid">
      <div class="content-column">
        <section class="section">
          <h2>I — Description</h2>
          <p>
            This discipline concerns the investigation of phenomena not fully explained by current scientific frameworks.
            It approaches such subjects through disciplined observation, critical analysis, and resistance to both blind belief and premature dismissal.
          </p>
          <p>
            Its purpose is not to affirm the extraordinary, but to examine it.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
          <h2>II — Fields of Inquiry</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>The nature and origin of celestial bodies and anomalies within our solar system</li>
            <li>The limits and potential of human perception, including claims of extrasensory awareness</li>
            <li>The reliability and transparency of institutional knowledge and authority</li>
            <li>The possibility of non-human intelligence and its relationship to humanity</li>
            <li>The historical accuracy and interpretation of ancient texts and traditions</li>
            <li>The existence of lost or undiscovered civilizations</li>
            <li>The question of whether humanity has reached its peak—or forgotten previous heights</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
          <h2>III — Open Questions</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>To what extent is human perception a reliable representation of reality?</li>
            <li>Can anomalous experiences be reduced to error alone, or do some point to overlooked structures of reality?</li>
            <li>What distinguishes a meaningful pattern from coincidence?</li>
            <li>Are there forms of intelligence not yet adequately recognized by current models?</li>
            <li>Do ancient records preserve observations that remain insufficiently understood?</li>
            <li>What is ignored when a phenomenon is dismissed before structured examination?</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
          <h2>IV — Research Frontiers</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Cross-analysis of historical and modern reports of unexplained phenomena</li>
            <li>Integration of anomalous claims with cognitive science and perception studies</li>
            <li>Structured documentation of subjective experience without surrendering analytical rigor</li>
            <li>Investigation of institutional bias toward unconventional data</li>
            <li>Comparative study of mythic, historical, and contemporary reports of non-human intelligence</li>
            <li>Examination of frontier questions concerning memory, signal, pattern, and interpretation</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
          <h2>V — Records of the Discipline</h2>

          <div class="records">
            <div class="record-block">
              <h4>Reports</h4>
              <p>No reports have yet been entered into the record.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="record-block">
              <h4>Observations</h4>
              <p>No observations are currently archived under this discipline.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="record-block">
              <h4>Essays</h4>
              <p>No essays have yet been submitted.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="record-block">
              <h4>Correspondence</h4>
              <p>No correspondence has yet been preserved in this section.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>


    </div>
  </main>






















</body>
</html>